    "reviewConclusions": [
      "The native tick result and old watermark are obtained before catalogue mutation; finite and strictly greater timestamp plus post-native exact lastTs equality are all required.",
      "Source composed through unchanged adaptBuildSource shows no-match and validOwnerClockTick rejection precede native lastTs assignment. Rejected future/prebind/session-clock packets therefore cannot update catalogue sidecar state.",
      "Duplicate and stale packets remain rejected even if post watermark equals their ts, because message.ts must be strictly above pre-call watermark.",
      "Remote actor identity, owner and life equality, packet shape and registered catalogue validation remain unchanged. Native return value is preserved.",
      "Scope is receiver-admission consistency; not a claim about Splatoon retail network internals or physical-device quality."
    ],
